      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-301271",
      ":question/problem": "A city randomly sampled $500$ residents about a proposed zoning plan. The results were categorized by age group and are shown below.\n\n|  | Plan to vote<br>for<br>Plan A | Plan to vote<br>for<br>Plan B |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Under $40$ | $180$ | $70$ |\n| $40 +$ | $130$ | $120$ |\n\nThe city has a total of $20,000$ eligible voters. Based on the table, what is the best estimate of the number of voters who plan to vote for Plan A?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
    },
